 "note": "C1: seeded clusters of trees, rocks, bushes and small props (lib/clusters.ts). Most scenery lives in clusters with bare ground between them; 'stray' is the share of the old uniform scatter that stays. 'enabled' true = clusters; false = the old scatter and lists exactly as before (one data edit and a deploy). 'anchors' are authored cluster centres (about two cairns round each landmark, plus the big groves and lines); 'cells' is a jittered grid per region: each cell holds a cluster with chance 'chance', of a kind weighted by 'mix', no closer than 'gap' m to another centre. Members of a cluster: n = [min,max] count (times the cluster size), zone = where (center, core, skirt, edge, line), s = scale range. A member takes its look from the real shapes only. 'props' says which small shapes a pool or line uses in that region. Metres. All values are first guesses to tune by eye: if still empty, raise chance by 0.1, then size, then lower gap by 2; if too busy, the reverse. The land rule (slope, dips, paths) is not in this slice: every site is accepted. 'gap' on a kind is the edge-to-edge space between its solid members (default: features minGap 1.6); the tight kinds (cairn, lone, thicket) use less than the player's width so they read as one solid lump rather than loose items.",
